From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:43:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: the gloves take the hands from the arms model, and
 its bind pose for the renderer

The gun run showed the game draws its first person hands as a model of
their own (hands/male/shared/v_shared_male_hands.mdl, view model 1)
whatever the weapon, while view model 0, the weapon, has zero or no hand
bones. The arms' cached bones are only remade with no weapon out. So the
hands now come only from the arms, only while their cache is this
frame's and not zero, and rt_vm_hands_bind gives the renderer each
hand's bind pose frame (the inverse of mstudiobone_t +0x60) with the
palm's middle and radius, so it can fit the hands from the arms' own
draws when the cache is stale. The probe logs both view models each
second.
